Design and implement a console-based music playlist in C++ using a doubly linked list. The user can add songs, move to the next or previous song, skip a song, undo the most recent skip, and display the playlist. When a song is skipped, it is not permanently deleted. Instead, the skipped song is stored in a skip history stack containing the last five skips. The undo operation restores the skipped song to its exact original position in the playlist.
